Our client, a leading Software, Information and Communication Technologies company, operates internationally (Athens, Brussels, Luxembourg, Copenhagen, Stockholm, London, Nicosia, Hong-Kong, Valetta, etc). Our client is a renowned supplier of IT services to government institutions, multinational corporations, public administrations and multinational companies, research and academic institutes.
﻿
Job Type: Full Time/Permanent
Location: EU
Workplace: Remote
Role Overview
Our client currently has a vacancy for an Enterprise Architect fluent in English, to offer his/her services as an expert remotely within the EU. In the context of the first assignment, the successful candidate will be integrated in the team of the company that will closely cooperate with a major client’s IT team on site.
Requirements

• Master’s degree in IT or relevant discipline, combined with minimum 17 years of relevant working experience in IT;

• At least 10 years of experience with enterprise architecture of large-scale organizations including leading and managing large scale distributed teams from diverse profiles;

• At least 10 years of specific expertise with the OECD templates and migration between versions of them and in the IUCLID product and plugins development;

• At least 10 years of specific expertise with IUCLID-based submission systems and Food systems;

• At least 10 years of specific expertise with Java programming language and single-page applications;

• At least 10 years of specific expertise with CQRS and Event-Sourcing architecture patterns leveraging distributed systems like Kafka;

• At least 10 years of specific expertise with Continuous integration/delivery and supporting tools like Jenkins, Azure pipelines and GitHub actions;

• At least 10 years of specific expertise with Agile methodologies and supporting tools like Confluence and Jira;

• Extensive experience with enterprise architecture best practices and goals and experience with analysis and design;

• Experience with modelling and graphical representations and abstractions;

• TOGAF Certification is a plus;

• Excellent command of the English language.

Responsibilities

• Create business architecture models that reflect the organization’s strategies and goals;

• Integrate the project and program strategies and ensure alignment with business strategies and drivers, and management priorities;

• Identify ways to reduce costs in IT and business leadership;

• Evaluate systems for discrepancies or vulnerabilities;

• Conduct research to find ways to improve operations;

• Provide business architecture and systems processing guidance;

• Create and implement a business vision and multi-year plan.

